p.seg:
I dislike 9) your common custom of saying things not true. To instance only in two or three particulars. You told Mr. Ireland,
James Ireland of Bristol (see the letter of Nov. 4, 1759
). ‘Mr. Vazeille learnt Spanish in a fortnight.’ You told Mr. Fry, ‘ Mrs. Ellison I.e., Susanna (Wesley) Ellison, JW’s sister. At this point Susanna (or ‘Suky’) was living in London. was the author as to my intrigue in Georgia.’ You told Mrs. Ellison ‘you never said any such thing; you never charged her with it.’ You also told her ‘that I had laid a plot to serve you as Susannah was served by the two elders.’ Referring to the story in the apocryphal book of Susanna, included by the Catholic Church in the book of Daniel .
